2026-09-27T10:25:37.6543571Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6544065Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6544536Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6545714Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6547085Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6547219Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6547504Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6547936Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6548605Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6548756Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6549048Z ================
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6549228Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6549451Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6550012Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6550323Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6550479Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6550872Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6551117Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6551330Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6551937Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6552583Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6553653Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6554581Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6554827Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6555513Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6556399Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6556883Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6557391Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6558094Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6558441Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6558755Z ========
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6558946Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6561154Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6563489Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6563859Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6564661Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6565922Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6649598Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6650640Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6651366Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6652293Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6652468Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6652875Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6653090Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6654750Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6656556Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6657551Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6659109Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:25:37.6659429Z 
